# macOS menu bar

- Ship as **accessory / LSUIElement** — no Dock, no Cmd-Tab app window for v1.
- Status item: left click = floating panel (toggle); right click = native menu (Done, Settings…, Quit); ⌥+click = Done when a one thing exists.
- Prefer SwiftUI for panel content; use AppKit for NSStatusItem, NSPanel, sound, etc. Do not use a transient `NSPopover` for the main UI (text editing breaks).
- Keep the panel small and power-user oriented — minimal chrome. Settings via native **⌘,** / **Settings…** (SwiftUI `Settings` scene; status-item menu uses the system Settings action).
- Panel window title is **Wedge** (system title bar); no in-content app title or Done button — Done is ⌘↩ / status-item shortcuts.
- List rows show an always-visible Notion-style **6-dot grip**; reorder via `List`/`onMove`.
- While panel/Settings is open, switch to `.regular` so the app menu exists; return to `.accessory` when idle.
